sxbar is a simple status bar for Xorg.

The package installs the executable as /usr/bin/sxbar and the example
configuration as /usr/share/sxbar/sxbarc. The upstream sxbar.1 file
is empty, so no manual page is installed.

At runtime, sxbar first looks for a user configuration in the XDG config
directories and then falls back to /usr/share/sxbar/sxbarc. Copy that
file to ~/.config/sxbar/sxbarc before customizing it.

sxbar uses X11, Xinerama, Xft, fontconfig, and freetype. These
libraries are provided by the Slackware base system.
